===Faction===
Faction in EverQuest represents how much a group of NPCs or creatures likes or dislikes your character. Most NPCs belong to one or more faction groups and is assigned to one primary faction. Your standing with a given faction has a meaningful impact on whether its members will assist you, ignore you, trade with you, offer quests, or attack you on sight.

Your standing with a given faction also depends on race, class, and sometimes deity. This value shift over time through your actions—primarily killing NPCs, completing quests, and finishing tasks or missions.

===How Factions Work===
Most NPCs belong to a specific faction or multiple factions. When you target them and enter "/con" into chat, you receive two pieces of information:

Their reaction toward you, as a measure of your modified standing with them

Their relative difficulty (combat strength)

An individually considered NPC’s (/con) Reaction to you ranges from deeply hostile to allied. Improving the primary faction the NPC belongs to typically requires helping that group or harming its enemies; harming a group usually benefits its rival factions.

Some NPCs will not speak to you, trade with you, or offer quests unless you reach a required attitude level. Others will attack immediately if your final standing with them is too low. This is called 'Kill on sight' or KOS.

